     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!<div><br></div><div>I am running into some issues with my yearly covariates in the UnmarkedMultFrame, and when running models and estimating detection with YEAR as a covariate.</div><div><br></div><div><u>I have set Year up as:</u></div><div><div>years.cov &lt;- data.frame(matrix(rep(2016:2017, each = nSites), nSites, 2))</div><div>years.cov &lt;- data.frame(lapply(years.cov, as.factor))</div></div><div><br></div><div><u>Put it into the UnmarkedFrame:</u></div><div><div>FosnUMF &lt;- unmarkedMultFrame(y = y, siteCovs = site.covs, obsCovs = list(obs.visit=obs.visit,obs.dayscore=obs.dayscore,obs.date=obs.date,obs.effort=obs.effort), numPrimary = T, <b>yearlySiteCovs = years.cov</b>)</div></div><div><br></div><div><u>Is this how Years are supposed to look in the summary() ?</u></div><div><div>Yearly-site-level covariates:</div><div>    X1        X2    </div><div> 2016:21   2017:21</div></div><div><br></div><div><u>When I try to model pformula ~years.cov, I need to unlist() the covariate to make it work:</u></div><div><div>  fm2 &lt;- colext(psiformula = ~1, gammaformula = ~1, epsilonformula = ~1, <b>pformula = ~unlist(years.cov)</b>, data = FosnUMF, se = TRUE)</div></div><div><br></div><div><u>I run into my main issue with predict() - Where Year is not treated as a category, and is mismatched compared to the detection estimates per year:</u></div><div><u><br></u></div><div><div>newdata.3 &lt;- data.frame(Year = as.character(2016:2017))</div><div><br></div><div>fm2.year &lt;- predict(fm2, newdata=newdata.3, type=&quot;det&quot;, appendData=TRUE)</div></div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt;   fm2.year</div><div>   Predicted         SE      lower     upper Year</div><div>1  0.1502292 0.08187875 0.04788491 0.3832624 2016</div><div>2  0.1502292 0.08187875 0.04788491 0.3832624 2017</div><div>3  0.1502292 0.08187875 0.04788491 0.3832624 2016</div><div>4  0.1502292 0.08187875 0.04788491 0.3832624 2017</div><div>5  0.1502292 0.08187875 0.04788491 0.3832